  "question": {
    "text": "Iodine reacts with concentrated <math><mi>H</mi><mi>N</mi><msub><mrow><mi>O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> to yield <math><mi>Y</mi></math> along with other products. The oxidation state of iodine in <math><mi>Y</mi></math> , is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>5</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>3</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>7</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>10&#160;</mn><mi>H</mi><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2&#160;</mn><mi>H</mi><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>10&#160;</mn><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>4&#160;</mn><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>O</mi></math><br /><br />Iodine gets oxidized to <math><mi>I</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi>O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math> when it reacts with an oxidizing agent <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>H</mi><mi>N</mi><msub><mrow><mi>O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math> The oxidation number of <math><mi>I</mi></math>&nbsp;in product will be<br /><br />Oxidation:&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>I</mi> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>I</mi><msubsup> <mi>O</mi> <mn>3</mn> <mo>&#8722;</mo> </msubsup> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></math><br /><br />Reduction: concentrated HNO<sub>3</sub>&nbsp;gives NO<sub>2</sub>.</p></blockquote>"
  }
